   "etymology": "Metathetic reduced form of dialectal britas (preserved in Gheg), extension in -as of brit- (stem for optative, admirative, participle, etc.); compare klith > këlthas, thirr > thërras, fol > flas, etc. From Proto-Albanian *breita, from Proto-Indo-European *bʰreyH- (“to cut, pierce”); cognate with Old Irish bríathar (“word”), Welsh brwydr (“fight, struggle”), and Russian брить (britʹ, “shave”). Related to brij.",
